  "question": {
    "text": "Function $x=A \\sin ^2 \\omega t+B \\cos ^2 \\omega t+C$ $\\sin \\omega t \\cos \\omega t$ represents SHM.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TGoiV",
      "text": "\nFor any value of $A, B$ and $C$ (except $C=0$ ) \n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ghqHD",
      "text": "\nIf $A=-B, C=2 B$, amplitude $=|B \\sqrt{2}|$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mcI5o",
      "text": "\nIf $A=B ; C=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wqkRq",
      "text": "\nIf $A=B ; C=2 B$, amplitude $=|B|$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $A=-B$ and $C=2 B$\n$$\nX=B \\cos 2 \\omega t+B \\sin 2 \\omega t=\\sqrt{2 B} \\sin \\left(2 \\omega t+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n$$\nThis is equation of SHM of amplitude $\\sqrt{2} B$\nIf $A=B$ and $C=2 B$, then $X=B+B \\sin 2 \\omega t$\nThis is also equation of SHM about the point $X=B$. Function oscillates between $X=0$ and $X=2 B$ with amplitude $B$.",
    "image": null
  },
